# Sweef @VERSION@ (ALPHA)

> **This is an alpha release.** Sweef is a young independent browser engine. Expect missing features,
> sites that do not render correctly, and rough edges. Sweef offers to open such pages in your system
> browser. Please do not rely on it for banking or other sensitive browsing yet.

Commit: `@COMMIT@`

## Install

| Platform | File | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Linux (Debian/Ubuntu) | `sweef_@VERSION@_linux_<arch>.deb` | `sudo apt install ./sweef_...deb` |
| Linux (Fedora/openSUSE) | `sweef_@VERSION@_linux_<arch>.rpm` | `sudo dnf install ./sweef_...rpm` |
| Linux (any) | `sweef_@VERSION@_linux_<arch>.AppImage` | `chmod +x` and run |
| Linux (any) | `sweef_@VERSION@_linux_<arch>.tar.gz`, or `install.sh` | user-level install, no root |
| macOS 12+ | `sweef_@VERSION@_darwin_universal.dmg` | @MAC_NOTE@ |
| Windows 10/11 | `sweef_@VERSION@_windows_<arch>_setup.exe` or `.zip` | @WIN_NOTE@ |

`<arch>` is `amd64` or `arm64`. Full instructions, uninstall steps and the unsigned-binary
workarounds are in [docs/install.md](https://github.com/sweefbrowser/sweef/blob/v@VERSION@/docs/install.md).

## Verify your download

```sh
sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS --ignore-missing
gh attestation verify <file> --repo sweefbrowser/sweef    # build provenance (SLSA)
```

## Known alpha limitations

- Installers are @SIGN_NOTE@
- No automatic updates yet: download the new version to update.
- See the README for rendering-fidelity numbers and known gaps.

